2089	    /// Remove a thread from the deterministic scheduler.  In order to call this, the precondition
2090	    /// is that this thread will execute no further (visible) instructions.
2091	    ///
2092	    /// This is called while the guest is running, not in the middle of a scheduler turn.
2093	    ///
2094	    /// This is IDEMPOTENT, and it may indeed be called twice, both to proactively remove a thread,
2095	    /// and then reactively in response to an exit hook.
